1
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:06,397
So Robin is in that
building behind you, huh?

2
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,560
Out of my way, bull guy!

3
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,550
Listen, boy.

4
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:12,640
Perhaps you haven't realized this,

5
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,660
but what you're doing right now is
nothing short of a world-class crime.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:30,940
Let's go.

7
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:14,677
I'll see

8
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:21,760
you

9
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:29,917
next time.

10
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,280
We won't go around the world!

11
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Start me up.

12
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,117
Let's go! Let's go!

13
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,897
Let's go! Let's go!

14
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:48,257
Let's go! Let's go!

15
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,380
Let's go!

16
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,737
Let's go! Let's go!

17
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:59,897
Let's go!

18
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:06,460
All right now, I'll
show you all in my heart

19
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:11,220
The new world, stop me up!

20
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,520
Stupid bastards!

21
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:37,190
Oh.

22
00:02:37,273 --> 00:02:38,103
Oh, I see.

23
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,500
Understood. So then,

24
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:48,837
when Sodom and his brother Gomorrah were
about to die in the belly of a sea king,

25
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,557
the Franky family showed up.

26
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:54,117
They were rescued and told these
fateful words that he still remembers.

27
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:57,259
Look, we're already full
so we're not gonna eat you.

28
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:58,757
And from that day forward,

29
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:01,817
the two brothers swore their
undying loyalty to their savior,

30
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:02,730
Franky.

31
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,977
So let me get this straight.

32
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,157
The Franky family brought down a sea king,

33
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,037
ate it, and they just
happened to be saved?

34
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:12,061
because Franky was already full?

35
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,240
Pretty much.

36
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,900
Fine, whatever.

37
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,037
You mind watching where you're going?

38
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,591
You're making me nervous.

39
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:25,100
I will follow big bro Franky
until the day I die, he says.

40
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:29,736
I bet he's really happy that one of
us can understand what he's saying.

41
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:39,780
He said, by the way,

42
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:42,437
the masked guy that was with you
never made it on board my back.

43
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,350
Is that OK?

44
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:48,970
Ah!

45
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,740
He's talking about Sniper King!

46
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:52,900
Where is he?

47
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,560
Why now? Why now?

48
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:58,130
Idiot.

49
00:03:58,213 --> 00:03:59,043
The fall off?

50
00:03:59,126 --> 00:04:00,060
Did you hear?

51
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,097
He hasn't been here from the start!

52
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:03,100
Don't tell me.

53
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,594
Did he run away again?

54
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,968
Arrogant pirates, you can't keep
this foolishness up forever!

55
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:20,037
If you want to pass, you'll
have to go through me to do it.

56
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:20,950
Fine then!

57
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,040
Is that really the best you've got?

58
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,979
Battleship cannon!

59
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:37,300
Come on!

60
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:39,037
There's only three of them!

61
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:39,950
Do something!

62
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:44,773
So, you're good at fighting, aren't you?

63
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:49,437
Then you can beat those guys, huh?

64
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,660
You bet.

65
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,160
We'll get her back.

66
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,909
We just needed motivation.

67
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,377
Now that we know Robin needs saving,

68
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:06,636
there's no limit to what Luffy and
the rest of our crew can accomplish.

69
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,920
I believe in him.

70
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,300
He can do it.

71
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:12,130
Go!

72
00:05:12,213 --> 00:05:13,080
Get that rope guy!

73
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,460
Not gonna happen.

74
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:19,840
Shrouds and Ratlander!

75
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:22,500
We're gone far!

76
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,920
Consider this a dead end.

77
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,240
Give up and go.

78
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,540
Just get to the point already.

79
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:44,200
The power of the world government
stretches across more than 170 nations.

80
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:47,899
This island is a symbol of
our strength and resolve.

81
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,937
Attacking it is not simply
an act of rebellion,

82
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:54,960
but a declaration of war against
every country in our alliance.

83
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:58,560
We are bound by our
honor to strike you down.

84
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,217
You will not only face a merciless death,

85
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,900
but serve as an example
to the entire world.

86
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,140
You're at most a few dozen men.

87
00:06:07,420 --> 00:06:10,137
You should have thought
this out more carefully.

88
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:11,860
I said out of my way!

89
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,381
So are you going to move or what?

90
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:16,517
It doesn't matter if I move or not.

91
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,617
The point is that you
condemned yourself to a death

92
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:21,157
sentence the second you
set foot on Endy's lobby.

93
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,416
You understand that?

94
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:24,327
Fighting is a waste of time.

95
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:27,697
You got a taste of our
strength at Iceberg's Mansion.

96
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:30,100
You cannot defeat our six powers.

97
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,520
The difference between
us is simply too great.

98
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,097
Yeah, maybe that's true.

99
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:42,900
But you know, for some reason, I have
a feeling I'm gonna win this time.

100
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,600
Here we go!

101
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,440
Iron Buddy.

102
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,200
Kum Kum Rifle!

103
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,857
This doesn't make any sense.

104
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,737
He wasn't like this at all
when I fought him before.

105
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:11,232
How is it that he's so much stronger now?

106
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,490
Goblin!

107
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:15,010
Chase!

108
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:47,280
I don't care about your honor or
your government or any of that.

109
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:49,698
You do what you want with that crap.

110
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:57,680
All that matters is
getting Robin out of here.

111
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,200
What are we going to do?

112
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,380
It's too late now.

113
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:17,859
Even if we wanted to, it's not like
we could go back and pick him up.

114
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:21,217
I'm sure he'll figure
out something or other.

115
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,837
But the whole island is
swarming with Marines.

116
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,449
He's not Luffy, after all.

117
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,297
He can't fight them off on his own.

118
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,397
Even if we don't realize it at first,

119
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:32,715
we've gotten stronger with
every challenge we've faced.

120
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:37,416
You may not think he's tough, but
he's survived as well as anyone else.

121
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:41,360
No one from our crew would die
at a time like this. Don't worry.

122
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:47,710
Look!

123
00:08:47,793 --> 00:08:49,524
We're almost to the courthouse!

124
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,252
This ought to stop them.

125
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:02,280
We've been hit! No!

126
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:03,620
Hold back!

127
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,160
We finally got one!

128
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:07,570
Sodom!

129
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:12,490
No!

130
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:13,490
This is bad!

131
00:09:13,573 --> 00:09:14,580
He needs my help!

132
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:16,860
Rip those teeth and hold on, Sodom!

133
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:18,420
You can't fall yet!

134
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:20,650
Guys!

135
00:09:20,733 --> 00:09:21,857
You're gonna have to jump!

136
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:22,940
Get off it quick!

137
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,400
Sodom can't go on!

138
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:29,593
That mortar hit him square in the chest!

139
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:31,054
He's about to go down!

140
00:09:31,660 --> 00:09:33,557
You gotta keep moving no matter what!

141
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,816
You're the only ones who can do this!

142
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,780
He says go!

143
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,720
He's coming down!

144
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,700
Nobody's riding it!

145
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:28,520
Where'd they go?

146
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,510
Come on.

147
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:34,600
Let's go, Gomorrah!

148
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:45,109
Why'd I have to not
land on that King Bull?

149
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,560
What am I going to do?

150
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,780
I'm way behind everyone else now.

151
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:54,268
These shipwrights are awesome, but I
should probably catch up with the others.

152
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:57,180
Then again, I did leave
the crew, didn't I?

153
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:59,326
Maybe I should just run away.

154
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:07,530
No!

155
00:11:07,613 --> 00:11:09,377
Running is the last thing I should do!

156
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:11,937
It doesn't matter whether I'm
a part of the crew or not.

157
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:14,297
I put on this disguise
so I can help my friends.

158
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:18,297
If Robin is willing to sacrifice herself
to save us, it's the least I can do.

159
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:20,145
My manhood's on the line here!

160
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,670
All right.

161
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:25,428
There's only one way to get back
to the others at this point.

162
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:28,937
I call it operation disguise
myself as one of the government

163
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:32,797
agents and walk straight to the
courthouse without anyone noticing.

164
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,700
Okay, let's do this.

165
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,840
Enemy attack!

166
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:42,940
Enemy attack!

167
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,497
They're flooding the island!

168
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:45,860
We're all gonna sink!

169
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,540
The giant woke up!

170
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:56,380
We tried for 50 years to pull it.

171
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:58,380
We let up on the town.

172
00:11:58,680 --> 00:12:00,092
You mean the government?

173
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:03,800
We're distressed to all
the giants in Elbath.

174
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:09,380
Elbath? Giants? Bosses?

175
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:12,140
Wait a sec.

176
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,317
Are you saying you're from Elbath?

177
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,341
Like the Warriors Village Elbath?

178
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:18,640
Who the hell are you, runt?

179
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:21,879
I'm Sniper King from Sniper Island.

180
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,026
I'm interested in your story.

181
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,573
By all means, continue.

182
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:27,500
Take your time.

183
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:32,444
There's not much point in telling
you, but I guess it can't hurt.

184
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:38,760
Kashi and I used to be
pirates a hundred years ago.

185
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,080
Our crew traveled the whole world.

186
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:44,880
But everything changed when
we visited a certain island.

187
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:49,517
Since they couldn't come to an
agreement, our two bosses started a duel.

188
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,260
We had to split up the crew.

189
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,700
We were at a loss.

190
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:55,377
All we could do was go
back to our hometowns.

191
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:57,720
A warrior's battle is life or death.

192
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:01,857
But as soon as it's over, the winner is
supposed to come back to their village.

193
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:05,540
We waited for 50 years and
never heard from either of them.

194
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:06,940
Something was wrong.

195
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:10,617
So Kashi and I set out
to sea to go back to the

196
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:13,297
island and find out what
happened with the duel.

197
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:16,556
But on our way there, we got
captured by some marines.

198
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:19,937
They forced us to answer all
kinds of questions about our crew.

199
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:21,457
Then we found out the truth.

200
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:24,160
Even though our bosses
were strong fighters,

201
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:29,302
they got caught by marines just like us
and were stuck in some big government jail.

202
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:33,000
All of that stuff happened
about 50 years ago.

203
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:35,820
The government made a deal with us.

204
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:40,608
They said if we would work for them for
100 years, they'd set our bosses free.

205
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:43,977
All we had to do was protect
and escape from intruders.

206
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:46,157
As long as we didn't let anyone through,

207
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:50,437
when our time was up, our bosses and
us could all go back to Elbaf together.

208
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:54,840
Since China's lived to be 300 or
so, we didn't think it was so bad.

209
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:58,962
So we agreed to the deal and kept
all of the bargain for 50 years.

210
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:02,717
But then those pirates came through
the gate and ruined everything.

211
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,329
That's why I'm so ashamed.

212
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,717
That's why I'm crying.

213
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:06,820
It's not fair.

214
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:11,937
Now our bosses are gonna be stuck in that
dumb prison for the rest of their lives.

215
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,120
Hey, hold on. Wait a second.

216
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,137
There's something funny about that story.

217
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:17,937
You think this is funny, you little jerk?

218
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:20,017
How dare you laugh at our pride?

219
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:23,840
I don't mean like funny
ha-ha, I mean funny weird.

220
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,677
Hey, what's so weird about it?

221
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:26,797
Before we came here,

222
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:31,056
my crew met those bosses of yours,
and we saw them fighting their duel.

223
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:36,274
Their names are Dorry and Broggy, right?

224
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:40,000
The warriors from Elbath, fighting
in an evenly matched duel,

225
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,140
over and over again, for a hundred years.

226
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:50,160
How do you know their names?

227
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:52,060
You must be lying.

228
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:56,181
If you need more proof than that,
I can tell you anything you want.

229
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,600
And then...

230
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:16,800
You still don't believe me?

231
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:18,568
What do I have to tell you?

232
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:24,920
They're weapons, maybe?

233
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:30,357
How they fight?

234
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:34,120
73,466 duels!

235
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:35,837
I know everything about them!

236
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:39,480
73,466 duels!

237
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,920
We really met them!

238
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:42,420
I swear it!

239
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:51,860
They weren't captured 50 years ago!

240
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:54,240
That's nothing but a big fat lie!

241
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:20,140
It's coming! Wait! Aim carefully!

242
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:22,660
Get it in your sights, men!

243
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:25,020
It's a trench mortar!

244
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:26,460
Gomorrah, dodge!

245
00:16:28,720 --> 00:16:30,357
Damn, bastards had an ammo.

246
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:31,400
waiting for us.

247
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:33,857
Taking the main road sure was a bad idea.

248
00:16:33,940 --> 00:16:35,180
Turn around, quick!

249
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:44,320
Not so fast!

250
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,617
Sorry, son of...

251
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,820
Stop right there!

252
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,470
Chopper.

253
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:10,020
Who could be calling?

254
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,880
Yes? Hello?

255
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:15,480
Howdy, howdy! Granny Kaku!

256
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:16,940
What's going on?

257
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:20,433
Alright, sounds like you're still alive.

258
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,937
There's a little something
I forgot to tell you.

259
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:25,457
I'm sure you're busy,
so I'll make it quick.

260
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:26,580
Listen carefully.

261
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:28,757
If you remember that map Polly drew,

262
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,617
you might notice there's no path from the

263
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,797
courthouse to the gates
of justice that's been.

